{"availability":"available","full":"Microtone-Project/Microtone.js","name":"Microtone.js","description":"A music tracker for the notes a piano cannot play. Any tuning on a 4096-step pitch grid, sources placed anywhere on the sphere, ambisonic B-format and stereo export.","category":"Productivity","language":"JavaScript","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-09T15:18:10Z","updated":"2026-10-09T18:57:46Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://microtone.cc","topics":["ambisonic","ambisonics","microtonal","microtonality","microtone","mod-tracker","music-composition","music-composition-software","spatial-music","tauri-app","tauri-v2","tracker-music","webapp"],"demo":"https://microtone.cc/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:03:59.983Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:03:59.983Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:03:59.983Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:07:09.950Z","stars":7,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-07T20:12:14.318Z","stars":7,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-09T22:03:59.983Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Microtone is a music tracker for the notes a piano cannot play. Every pitch sits on a grid of 4096 steps per octave, so 12-TET, 19-TET, 31-TET, Bohlen–Pierce and a temperament you drew yourself are all the same kind of thing to it. Sources can be placed anywhere on the sphere and delivered as ambisonic B-format as readily as stereo. It runs in a browser tab, and that is the entire install."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"13eb4cf8d062979f1e906c706e6cb37bb45fc89725006aec9871c340d44a3c15","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:17.097Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:17.097Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Microtone is a music tracker for the notes a piano cannot play. Every pitch sits on a grid of 4096 steps per octave, so 12-TET, 19-TET, 31-TET, Bohlen–Pierce and a temperament you drew yourself are all the same kind of thing to it. Sources can be placed anywhere on the sphere and delivered as ambisonic B-format as readily as stereo. It runs in a browser tab, and that is the entire install.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"There is no account and no server side — projects live in your browser's private storage, and even MIDI and module conversion happens on your own machine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign-in is SceneID OAuth (server/online/sceneid.js); its client id and secret are Worker secrets (npx wrangler secret put) and live in .dev.vars beside wrangler.toml locally — never in a committed file, since everything tracked here is public.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The desktop app (desktop/) signs in through the system's browser instead of a pop-up (server/online/desktop.js): its sign-in runs on this site as usual, then hands the app a one-time code through the app's cc.microtone.desktop: scheme, which the app swaps — with a PKCE verifier only it holds — for an access token it sends as Authorization: Bearer.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"13eb4cf8d062979f1e906c706e6cb37bb45fc89725006aec9871c340d44a3c15","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:17.098Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T18:57:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Microtone-Project/Microtone.js/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:17.099Z","hash":"13eb4cf8d062979f1e906c706e6cb37bb45fc89725006aec9871c340d4